<BaseLayout title="About & academic background" description="Academic background and research interests of Isaac Daroch: computer engineering, international study experience and doctoral work in Advanced Systems Engineering."><section class="section"><div class="shell about-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT / ISAAC DAROCH</p><h1>Building systems.<br/><em>Questioning models.</em></h1><p class="lead">I am a computer engineer and PhD student in Advanced Systems Engineering at Universidad Andrés Bello, Chile.</p><p>My interests connect artificial intelligence, representations of the world, continual learning and autonomous agents. I also teach data mining, econometrics and data visualization.</p><p>I completed postgraduate training in computer engineering and took part in international study at TU Ilmenau through DAAD. My work has included applied software, data and digital-health systems.</p><p class="method-note">Biographical statements are supplied by the site owner. They are not independently credential-verified by this software. Research interests and future ambitions are distinct from published results.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/publications/">Publication records ↗</a><a class="button button-ghost" href="/projects/">Experiments ↗</a></div></div><figure class="portrait"><img src="/images/portrait.png" alt="Portrait used on Isaac Daroch’s public GitHub profile" width="512" height="512" loading="eager"/><figcaption>Profile portrait · reused with the portfolio owner’s request. Some portfolio portraits were prepared with AI assistance.</figcaption></figure></div></section><Contact/></BaseLayout>
